  "notes": "verify-B4 rerun 2026-10-25 on umbriel-b200-018, harness 0.8 (card: 0.4), source exp/topk-swarm/B4 commit d55e2cd430, control B1_n6b (approaches/B1 from the same tree), all 24 cells x 2 regimes of the card (N 1024, 4096 x k 16, 64, 256, both requirements), batch state/results/verify-B4/N9_w2fin2_vs_B1_n6b_focus_vb4_n9b_20261025_171436.json, named control in one lock section, canaries 32.00098 and 3780 to 3782 us, oracle 22 battery cases passed per cell for variant and control (card: 13). VERDICT verified = true. The card's three claims reproduce as conclusions (rerun | card, cycles per call): k 16 kill cells bf16 not_guaranteed N 1024 1725 against 1701 (plus 1.4 percent) and N 4096 2570 against 2539 (plus 1.2) | plus 2.1 and 2.9, the 15 percent kill criterion is not met either way. k 64 to 256 not_guaranteed minus 6 to 18.5 percent (bf16 N 1024 k 64 1840 against 2138, k 256 1980 against 2429, N 4096 k 64 3130 against 3801, k 256 3767 against 4464. fp32 1875 against 1992, 2006 against 2334, 3344 against 3763, 4012 against 4517) | minus 5 to 17. prefer_smaller_index minus 5 to 42 percent (bf16 N 1024 k 16 1970 against 2172, k 64 1996 against 2662, k 256 2050 against 2921, N 4096 k 16 3226 against 3808, k 64 3471 against 5961, k 256 4068 against 6946. fp32 N 1024 k 16 1966 against 2072, N 4096 k 64 3856 against 5069, k 256 4428 against 6032) | minus 7 to 41. Cells outside the 3 percent ratio tolerance, all but one in N9's favor: bf16 N 1024 k 64 and 256 not_guaranteed and fp32 N 1024 k 256 not_guaranteed (ratio plus 3.8 to 5.3 percent, the B1_n6b control is 4.2 to 4.7 percent above the card there while its k 16 cells match within 1.5 percent, cause not isolated, node or the 0.6 chain rotation on a data-dependent second pass), bf16 N 4096 k 256 not_guaranteed and k 16 and 256 prefer_smaller_index (plus 3.3 to 8.1 percent: the variant is 6 to 9 percent below the card at bf16 N 4096, the harness-version effect on striped loads at IPT 16 documented in card B4_v4_b200_20261025_2), and bf16 N 1024 k 16 prefer_smaller_index minus 4.4 percent (1.10x against 1.15x, the low edge of the prefer_smaller_index range is 9 percent here instead of the card's 13). Throughput within 0.2 percent everywhere. T57 same-kernel A/B against N9_w2fin (consecutive lock sections, B1_n6b within 1.5 percent): the class-indexed ticket saves 52 to 1189 cycles per call (3 to 24 percent), card 48 to 1070. One low-level claim does not reproduce under 0.8: the card gives 40 registers for the bf16 N 1024 latency kernel against N9_w2fin's 46, the rerun has 46 for both (throughput kernels 40 for both in both builds), with the SASS instruction counts of the card (2536 against 2680 at bf16 N 1024 k 16, 5968 against 6552 at N 4096 k 256), so the instruction-count evidence for the removed aggregation sequence stands and the register attribution does not. Chain fits r2 >= 0.991. Zero spill everywhere. The B1_n6b control's 4 to 5 percent at N 1024 k 64 and 256 has the same root cause, confirmed by eval-engineer on 2026-10-25 (harness README section 3.1): under the 0.6 rotation the min over repetitions picked the cheaper half of the inputs at chain 8 for a kernel whose pass count depends on the input, fixed in harness 0.10 by fixed strided input subsets per chain length. It is a harness effect, not a node effect."
